        {
          "title": "Save the Project in your own Workspace Directory",
          "description": "<span style=\"font-size: 0.9rem;\">Choose a destination folder and confirm. VS Code will copy the sample files into your new application folder.</span><div><br><div>⚠️ <strong>Keep your workspace path short.</strong> <strong style=\"font-size: 0.9rem;\">Recommendation:</strong><span style=\"font-size: 0.9rem;\"> place your application in a short root path, for example </span><code dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color: rgb(14, 138, 125);\">C:\\nordic\\workspace\\hello_world</code></div><div><font color=\"#0e8a7d\" face=\"IBM Plex Mono, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.672px;\"><br></span></font><div><span style=\"font-size: 14.4px;\">Once you've confirmed the path by pressing Enter, you can choose whether to open a new VS Code instance (“Open in New Window”) or to display the project in the current instance (“Open”).&nbsp;</span></div><div><br><div><br></div></div></div></div>",
          "codeBlocks": [],
